{
  "kind": "attack8",
  "comment": "Pose guides for the 8-direction, 6-frame attack sheet; conventions as walk8.json. Six frames of anticipation, strike and recovery: guard, wind back with the weight on the rear foot, the swing coming through high, full extension over a lunge, the follow-through swept down across the body, and a recovery back towards guard. The right arm carries the weapon because at a left-facing profile the character's right side is the one towards the camera, and the swing is cross-body rather than a straight thrust on purpose -- a thrust along the facing axis is invisible in the rows that face the camera, where a cross-body arc still sweeps the whole width of the cell. Frames 2 and 4 are the pair a viewer has to be able to tell apart at 32px, so one puts the weapon hand high and forward and the other puts it low and across.",
